# Configuration of the Grafana dashboard linter.
#
# See https://github.com/grafana/dashboard-linter. Run via
# `make -C modules/monitoring lint-dashboard`.
#
# The linter encodes the conventions of the Grafana mixins. The rules below are
# the ones Blaze deliberately doesn't follow. Everything else is enabled and has
# to pass.
exclusions:
  panel-title-description-rule:
    reason: >-
      Most panels only have a title. Descriptions are added as the panels get
      documented, not as a precondition for linting.

  template-job-rule:
    reason: >-
      The job variable is single select on purpose. The dashboard shows one
      Blaze instance at a time, so panels like the RocksDB ones would mix
      unrelated series if several jobs could be selected at once.

  template-instance-rule:
    reason: >-
      Same as template-job-rule. The instance variable is single select because
      the dashboard shows one instance at a time.

  uneditable-dashboard:
    reason: >-
      The dashboard is published as a release asset and imported by users. It
      has to stay editable so that they can adapt it. The source of truth is
      dashboard.edn, not the imported copy.
